---
// The accessibility statement (audit-a11y round 1, B1): every claim here is true of the build.
// `npm run build:production` runs the axe suite (tests/browser/axe.mjs) and stops on a failure;
// the date below is the last time the statement was reviewed against the site.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
const turnstile = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY);
---
<Base title="Accessibility" description="How theluxuryliners.com is built to be accessible, what is known not to work yet, and how to tell us about a problem.">
  <PageHead title="Accessibility" size="l">
    <p class="lede">We want everyone to be able to use this site. It aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA.</p>
  </PageHead>
  <div class="wrap page-body">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h3">Status</h2>
      <p>We believe the site partially conforms to WCAG 2.2 level AA: most of it meets the standard, and the parts that may not are listed under “Known limitations”. This statement was last reviewed on <time datetime="2026-11-06">November 6, 2026</time>.</p>
      <h2 class="h3">What we do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>{turnstile ? 'Every page except the contact form works without JavaScript; the contact form’s spam check needs it.' : 'Every page works without JavaScript.'} Every page works with the keyboard alone and on small screens.</li>
        <li>Every photo has a text description; every cover is named.</li>
        <li>Links in running text are underlined. Menus, buttons and cards are marked by their shape and place on the page, and the keyboard focus is always visible.</li>
        <li>There is a light and a dark theme. The site follows your device’s setting, and the “Dark theme” switch at the top of each page (it needs JavaScript) changes it.</li>
        <li>Animations are switched off when your device asks for reduced motion.</li>
        <li>Videos load only when you press play.</li>
        <li>Before each release, every page is checked with the axe accessibility engine, in both themes, at desktop and phone widths. The production build stops if a page fails.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="h3">Known limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Videos play in YouTube’s player, which we do not control. Its captions and controls are YouTube’s.</li>
        {turnstile && <li>The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to stop spam. It needs JavaScript, and on rare occasions it may ask you to confirm you are human.</li>}
        <li>Words that appear inside cover art, flyers and old photos are described in the text around them, not transcribed in full.</li>
        <li>Automated checks find only some problems. If something gets in your way, please tell us.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="h3">Tell us about a problem</h2>
      <p>If something on the site doesn’t work for you, please use the <a href="/contact/?topic=accessibility">contact form</a> and choose “Accessibility problem”. Tell us the page and what happened. We aim to reply within 10 working days.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
